The returned string is empty when the user cancels the dialog. The initial directory parameter is connected to the JC Lib folder browser.

Previous workflow example retained from the original Qt pack:

```cpp
const QString fileName = QFileDialog::getOpenFileName(
    this,
    tr("Open configuration"),
    QDir::homePath(),
    tr("JSON files (*.json);;All files (*)"));

if (!fileName.isEmpty())
{
    loadConfiguration(fileName);
}
```

Returns an empty QStringList when canceled.

Previous workflow example retained from the original Qt pack:

```cpp
const QStringList files = QFileDialog::getOpenFileNames(
    this,
    tr("Select log files"),
    QDir::homePath(),
    tr("Log files (*.log *.txt);;All files (*)"));

for (const QString &fileName : files)
{
    importLog(fileName);
}
```

The selected path may not exist yet. The initial output path parameter uses the JC Lib file browser.

Previous workflow example retained from the original Qt pack:

```cpp
const QString fileName = QFileDialog::getSaveFileName(
    this,
    tr("Export report"),
    QDir::homePath() + "/report.csv",
    tr("CSV files (*.csv);;All files (*)"));

if (!fileName.isEmpty())
{
    exportReport(fileName);
}
```

The initial directory parameter uses the JC Lib folder browser.

Previous workflow example retained from the original Qt pack:

```cpp
const QString directory = QFileDialog::getExistingDirectory(
    this,
    tr("Choose output directory"),
    QDir::homePath());

