functions.longDescription:
Context properties are convenient for small applications. For reusable modules and larger projects, prefer registered QML types or singletons with explicit module interfaces.

Previous workflow example retained from the original Qt QML pack:

```cpp
class Backend : public QObject
{
    Q_OBJECT
    Q_PROPERTY(QString status READ status NOTIFY statusChanged)
public:
    QString status() const { return status_; }
signals:
    void statusChanged();
private:
    QString status_ = QStringLiteral("Idle");
};

Backend backend;
engine.rootContext()->setContextProperty("backend", &backend);
```

Connect objectCreationFailed before loading when application startup must fail cleanly. The original complete startup workflow remains attached below.

Previous workflow example retained from the original Qt QML pack:

```cpp
QGuiApplication app(argc, argv);
QQmlApplicationEngine engine;
const QUrl url(u"qrc:/qml/Main.qml"_qs);
QObject::connect(&engine, &QQmlApplicationEngine::objectCreationFailed,
                 &app, []() { QCoreApplication::exit(-1); }, Qt::QueuedConnection);
engine.load(url);
return app.exec();
```

