functions.longDescription:
Validate spy.isValid() after construction. The retained workflow shows how to verify emitted arguments.

Previous workflow example retained from the original Qt pack:

```cpp
QSignalSpy spy(controller, &DeviceController::measurementReady);
QVERIFY(spy.isValid());
controller->startMeasurement();
QVERIFY(spy.wait(1000));
QCOMPARE(spy.count(), 1);
```

QCOMPARE integrates with Qt Test reporting and is preferable to Q_ASSERT inside test functions.

Previous workflow example retained from the original Qt pack:

```cpp
QCOMPARE(result.status(), DeviceStatus::Ready);
QCOMPARE(result.value(), 42);
QVERIFY(result.isValid());
```

Prefer QTRY_VERIFY-style macros over hard-coded sleeps for asynchronous tests.

Previous workflow example retained from the original Qt pack:

```cpp
controller->startMeasurement();
QTRY_VERIFY_WITH_TIMEOUT(controller->isIdle(), 3000);
```

Declare matching columns in the associated _data function with QTest::addColumn<T>().

Previous workflow example retained from the original Qt pack:

```cpp
void DeviceControllerTest::parse_data()
{
    QTest::addColumn<QByteArray>("frame");
    QTest::addColumn<int>("expectedCount");

    QTest::newRow("single") << QByteArray("A") << 1;
    QTest::newRow("triple") << QByteArray("ABC") << 3;
}

void DeviceControllerTest::parse()
{
    QFETCH(QByteArray, frame);
    QFETCH(int, expectedCount);
    QCOMPARE(parseFrame(frame).size(), expectedCount);
}
```

Use Qt Test input helpers for deterministic GUI interaction tests.

Previous workflow example retained from the original Qt pack:

```cpp
QTest::mouseClick(button, Qt::LeftButton);
QCOMPARE(label->text(), QStringLiteral("Running"));
```

Keep setup outside the benchmark block when it must not contribute to the measured cost.

Previous workflow example retained from the original Qt pack:

```cpp
QBENCHMARK
{
    ParseFrame(payload);
}
```

